+# DOM Identity Scantling
+
+## Contract
+
+When a user interaction changes a todo item's state (completed ↔ uncompleted,
+editing activation/deactivation, title edit), the application MUST mutate the
+existing `<li>` DOM node in-place rather than replacing it via full list rebuild.
+
+## Seam: `render` in `js/app.js`
+
+The `render` function MUST NOT replace the `.todo-list` children when only
+individual item state has changed. The following are forbidden:
+
+- `todoList.innerHTML = '<entire new content>'`
+- `todoList.replaceChildren()`
+- Any equivalent full-replacement pattern
+
+Allowed: per-node mutations such as:
+- `li.classList.add('completed')` / `li.classList.remove('completed')`
+- `checkbox.checked = true` / `checkbox.checked = false`
+- `label.textContent = newTitle`
+
+## Affected paths
+
+Every state-change entry point that currently calls `this.render()` MUST instead
+apply an in-place DOM mutation:
+
+| Method        | Current behaviour              | Required behaviour                        |
+|---------------|--------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|
+| `toggleTodo`  | `render()` replaces all `<li>` | Toggle `completed` class + checkbox only  |
+| `toggleAll`   | `render()` replaces all `<li>` | Toggle `completed` class + checkbox on each `<li>` |
+| `removeTodo`  | `render()` replaces all `<li>` | Remove the single `<li>` node             |
+| `commitEdit`  | `render()` replaces all `<li>` | Update `label.textContent` + clear editing class |
+| `cancelEdit`  | `render()` replaces all `<li>` | Restore `label.textContent` + clear editing class |
+| `clearCompleted` | `render()` replaces all `<li>` | Remove each completed `<li>` node        |
+
+The `.todo-count`, `#toggle-all` checked state, and `#main`/`#footer` visibility
+may still be updated via direct DOM references — they do not require a full list
+rebuild.
+
+## Why this matters
+
+A full list rebuild (`innerHTML = ''`) destroys the existing DOM nodes. In a
+real browser, any reference held before the rebuild (such as a Cypress chain
+subject, a blur-event handler's `closest('li')` lookup, or a focus reference)
+becomes detached from the live document. This causes:
+
+1. DOM detachment errors on chained commands
+2. Spurious `blur` events during the rebuild that overwrite intent (e.g., cancel
+   edit → blur fires → edit is saved despite Escape key)
+3. Index mismatches when a re-render occurs between event dispatch and handler
+   completion
\ No newline at end of file
